     {
      "type": "mainHeadline",
      "text": "Essentials of Barcelona",
      "variant": "HEADING_XL",
      "id": "/lh/en/mobile-app/europe/essentials-of-barcelona_title",
      "isBold": true
     },
     {
      "type": "copyText",
      "text": "<b>21. June 2025 | 2 min read | Lufthansa Editorial Team</b>",
      "size": "SMALL",
      "variant": "BODY",
      "id": "/lh/en/mobile-app/europe/essentials-of-barcelona_info"
     },
     {
      "type": "copyText",
      "text": "<b>Here you can swim and admire unfinished buildings: five things about Barcelona that will surprise you.</b>",
      "size": "MEDIUM",
      "variant": "BODY",
      "id": "/lh/en/mobile-app/europe/essentials-of-barcelona_description_0"
     },
     {
      "type": "spacer",
      "size": "MEDIUM",
      "id": "/lh/en/mobile-app/europe/essentials-of-barcelona_separator"
     },
     {
      "type": "copyText",
      "text": "<b>A Missed Opportunity</b>",
      "size": "MEDIUM",
      "variant": "BODY",
      "id": "/lh/en/mobile-app/europe/essentials-of-barcelona_paragraph_0"
     },
     {
      "type": "copyText",
      "text": "Barcelona could have outdone Paris with an “Eiffel Tower” – almost. The story that Gustave Eiffel first offered his tower to the Catalonian capital is just a legend. But what is true is that Barcelona rejected three projects that were quite similar to the Eiffel Tower for the 1888 World’s Fair. The Parisians, however, said “oui” to Gustave Eiffel and his tower for their World’s Fair a year later – and, as it turned out, to one of the most iconic landmarks in history.",
      "size": "MEDIUM",
      "variant": "BODY",
      "id": "/lh/en/mobile-app/europe/essentials-of-barcelona_paragraph_1"
     },
     {
      "type": "image",
      "id": "/content/mobile/lh/en/articles/essentials-of-barcelona/jcr:content/articlecontentfragment/par1/image",
      "url": "https://www.lufthansa.com/content/dam/lh/article-images/mobile-app/europe/essentials-of-barcelona/lh_blog_barcelona_illustration1_sylvia-neuner_1920x1080.jpg.transform/lh-dcep-transform-width-1440/img.jpg",
      "contentDescription": "Illustration: Gustave Eiffel holding a plan of the Eiffel Tower next to a cityscape of Barcelona"
     },
     {
      "type": "copyText",
      "text": "<b>Award-Winning Architecture</b>",
      "size": "MEDIUM",
      "variant": "BODY",
      "id": "/lh/en/mobile-app/europe/essentials-of-barcelona_paragraph_2"
     },
     {
      "type": "copyText",
      "text": "The Royal Institute of British Architects awards the Royal Gold Medal for Architecture to individuals who have made outstanding contributions to the field. An exception was made for Barcelona – in 1999, for the first and only time to date, the award was given to an entire city.",
      "size": "MEDIUM",
      "variant": "BODY",
      "id": "/lh/en/mobile-app/europe/essentials-of-barcelona_paragraph_3"
     },
     {
      "type": "spacer",
      "size": "MEDIUM",
